slations of the unembeddings, therefore one might hope that centering the unembeddings might help, since the cosine similarity of the centered unembeddings is translation invariant. However, as we show in Section 3.2 below, this does still not give us a guarantee of high cosine similarity leading to high probabilities for the same inputs and also does not give us a guarantee that low cosine similarities will lead to low probabilities for the same inputs. We will also show in Section 3.3 below that fixing the length of the unembeddings is also not enough to get a guarantee.
